WEBVTT

NOTE
Acme Robotics — Fremont pilot standup (recorded)
Thursday, October 9, 8:32 AM PT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.500
<v Priya Shah>Quick one today — three things: fleet software, the cert
package, and visitor day prep. Fleet first.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
<v Priya Shah>WMS task-feed integration is running against their test
environment since Tuesday. Four hundred simulated picks overnight, zero
dropped tasks. That risk is basically retired.

3
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:24.000
<v Tom Okafor>Good. Less good: units 07 and 08 are throwing intermittent
e-stop faults on the v0.4 Orin firmware. Roughly one fault per three-hour
bench run, no pattern yet.

4
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:34.000
<v Tom Okafor>The problem isn't the fault itself, it's the paperwork. The
R15.08 package has to include clean safety-function test logs — e-stop and
interlock — and we cannot generate those logs while the firmware is
faulting.

5
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:41.000
<v Priya Shah>So that's a new blocker: the safety certification package
is blocked on a firmware fix for the e-stop faults. How long to
root-cause?

6
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:49.000
<v Tom Okafor>If it's the watchdog timing change from v0.4, two days to fix
and one clean 24-hour run to prove it. If it's hardware, longer. I'd call
it a real risk to the cert milestone, not a scare.

7
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:57.000
<v Marcus Webb>Then log it in the risk register as e-stop faults blocking
the safety certification test logs. The package date is already tight
against the November go-live, and I don't want to find out on the 16th
that we have no test logs to attach.

8
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:04.000
<v Priya Shah>Agreed. Tom owns the root-cause on the e-stop faults, daily
update in the channel until it's closed.

9
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:11.000
<v Marcus Webb>Visitor day: agenda is final, training session three is
tomorrow at seven. Associates are asking good questions — that part is
going well.

10
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Priya Shah>That's everything. Back to it — thanks all.
